#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:2
msgid "PyBaMM model zoo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:4
msgid ""
"Community- and partner-contributed PyBaMM models. One folder per model, "
"holding its code, tests, examples, citation, and a declarative `model.toml` "
"manifest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:7
msgid ""
"The manifest is the only boilerplate you write. The registry, the contract "
"test suite, the docs page, the CI routing, and the status badge are all "
"derived from it. Manifests are parsed, never imported, so a model whose "
"dependencies are missing still appears in the registry and the docs and "
"reports a clean failure rather than taking the zoo down."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:13
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:15
msgid ""
"The zoo is released to PyPI independently of PyBaMM, so `pip install pybamm` "
"does not provide it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:18
msgid "pip install pybamm-model-zoo\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:22
msgid ""
"A model with third-party dependencies of its own declares them as an extra "
"named `zoo-<slug>`, and the `zoo-all` extra installs every model's:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:25
msgid "pip install \"pybamm-model-zoo[zoo-all]\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:29
msgid ""
"Every model supports the PyBaMM releases the zoo's own `pybamm` requirement "
"admits, so `pip` only installs a PyBaMM they all work with."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:32
msgid ""
"In a PyBaMM checkout the zoo is a `uv` workspace member, so `uv sync --extra "
"all --group dev` from the repository root installs it editable alongside "
"`pybamm`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:36
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:38
msgid ""
"import pybamm\n"
"import pybamm_model_zoo as zoo\n"
"\n"
"zoo.list_models()\n"
"entry = zoo.info(\"LinearisedSPM\")\n"
"entry.tier, entry.maintainers\n"
"\n"
"model = zoo.load(\"LinearisedSPM\")()\n"
"solution = pybamm.Simulation(model).solve([0, 300])\n"
"print(solution[\"Voltage [V]\"](150))\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:51
msgid ""
"Using a model registers its citation, so `pybamm.print_citations()` credits "
"its authors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:54
msgid "Adding a model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:56
msgid ""
"[!IMPORTANT] Before adding a model, please read the [model zoo policy]"
"(https://github.com/pybamm-team/PyBaMM/blob/main/packages/pybamm-model-zoo/"
"POLICY.md). By opening a pull request that adds or changes a model in the "
"zoo, you agree to the policy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:59
msgid ""
"nox -s zoo-new -- --slug my_model --name MyModel --author \"A. Author\" --"
"github ahandle\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:63
msgid ""
"That renders [`template/`](https://github.com/pybamm-team/PyBaMM/tree/main/"
"packages/pybamm-model-zoo/template) into `src/pybamm_model_zoo/my_model/` "
"and appends your `.github/CODEOWNERS` line, so changes to your folder "
"request you as reviewer. The rendered skeleton passes the whole contract "
"suite as generated — the zoo's own test suite renders the template and runs "
"every check against the result, so that is a tested claim rather than a hope."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:70
msgid "Then:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:72
msgid "Replace the TODOs in `model.toml`, `README.md`, and `CITATION.bib`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:73
msgid "Put your physics in `model.py`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:74
msgid ""
"Write at least one test that pins a **physical** result — a known limit, an "
"analytic solution, a conservation check, or a published figure. That the "
"model merely runs is already covered by the contract suite, so a test that "
"only checks it runs adds nothing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:78
msgid "Regenerate the docs: `nox -s zoo-docs`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:79
msgid "Run it: `nox -s zoo -- --zoo-model=my_model`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:80
msgid ""
"Add a bullet to this package's `CHANGELOG.md`. Zoo pull requests never touch "
"PyBaMM's changelog."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:83
msgid ""
"[`linearised_spm/`](https://github.com/pybamm-team/PyBaMM/tree/main/packages/"
"pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/linearised_spm) is the reference "
"entry: the smallest thing that is still a real model. Copy that folder "
"rather than reading prose."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:87
msgid "Dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:89
msgid ""
"A model's dependencies are declared in one place: a per-model **optional** "
"extra named `zoo-<slug>` (dashes, not underscores) in this package's "
"`pyproject.toml`, listed in the `zoo-all` aggregate — never in the base "
"dependencies. Workspace members share one lockfile and one dev venv, so a "
"base dependency here lands in every contributor's environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:95
msgid ""
"For a PyBaMM feature with optional dependencies of its own, depend on "
"PyBaMM's extra rather than the packages behind it, so their versions stay "
"PyBaMM's to pin:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:98
msgid "zoo-my-model = [\"pybamm[fem]\"]\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:102
msgid ""
"The registry reads the extra from the installed package metadata. "
"`zoo.load()` checks it before importing your model, and the template's "
"`pybamm_model_zoo.require(SLUG)` checks it when the model is created, so a "
"missing extra fails straight away with the `pip install` that fixes it, "
"however the model was imported. Keep that call first in your `__init__`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:108
msgid ""
"The aggregate is deliberately not called `all`: `uv sync --extra all` "
"applies the extra to every workspace member that defines one, so an `all` "
"extra here would drag every model's heavy dependencies into the core dev "
"environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:112
msgid "PyBaMM versions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:114
msgid ""
"Every model shares the zoo's one PyBaMM floor, its `pybamm>=` requirement in "
"`pyproject.toml`. If your model needs a newer PyBaMM, raise the floor in the "
"same pull request. The release workflow builds and solves every model "
"against the floor before publishing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:119
msgid "Tiers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid "Tier"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid "Who sets it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid "CI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid "`community`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid "the default for a new model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid ""
"Runs on every pull request, **advisory**: reports red without blocking a "
"merge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid "`core`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid "PyBaMM maintainers, by adopting a model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid ""
"Runs in PyBaMM's merge gate. A failure blocks a merge, in core and in the "
"zoo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:126
msgid ""
"Advisory-ness lives in the CI job, never in an `xfail` marker: a community "
"model that fails, fails, and that is exactly the signal its badge reports. "
"Being advisory is what lets the zoo test contributed models on every pull "
"request without a contributed model ever blocking a PyBaMM release. The "
"manifest tier is what puts a model's tests behind the `gating` marker, and "
"what `--zoo-tier=core` keeps out of the merge gate's collection entirely."
msgstr ""

