#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:143
msgid "The contract"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:145
msgid ""
"`pybamm_model_zoo.testing.contract.CHECKS` is the one definition of the "
"contract: the test suite, the manifest's `skip_contract` validation, and "
"this table all derive from it. Each check has a **scope**, which is what "
"lets the same module hold an in-tree model and a third-party collection to "
"the right rules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid "Check"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid "Scope"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid "What it asserts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid "`manifest`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid "model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid ""
"Schema valid; `slug` matches the folder name; `class` is parseable; at least "
"one maintainer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid "`layout`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid ""
"`README.md`, `CITATION.bib`, `examples/`, and `tests/` present, and the "
"README has `Summary`, `Usage`, `Validation`, and `Citation` sections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid "`import`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid ""
"The declared class imports and subclasses `pybamm.BaseModel`. Skipped with a "
"reason when your `zoo-<slug>` extra is not installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid "`citation`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid ""
"The manifest's citation key resolves in your `CITATION.bib`, and "
"instantiating the model registers it, so `pybamm.print_citations()` credits "
"you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid "`well_posed`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid "`model.check_well_posedness()` passes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid "`build`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid "`pybamm.Simulation(model).build()` succeeds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid "`solve`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid ""
"The model solves for the manifest's `solve_time`, and every `key_variables` "
"entry is finite read through the interpolating call interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid "`packaging`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid "packaging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid ""
"An in-tree model is importable as `pybamm_model_zoo.<slug>`, and `zoo-all` "
"includes its extra if it has one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid "`license`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid ""
"An in-tree model's manifest says `BSD-3-Clause`, the zoo package's license. "
"Cannot be waived."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid "`docs`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid "repo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid ""
"The generated docs page is present *and current*, so docs cannot drift from "
"code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid "`codeowners`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/contributing.md:7
msgid ""
"`.github/CODEOWNERS` names an owner for your folder, so ownership cannot be "
"dropped silently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:164
msgid ""
"A third-party collection is held only to the `model` scope; it is not wired "
"into this package and does not live in this repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:167
msgid ""
"`skip_contract` waives an individual check for a genuinely unusual model — "
"one with no meaningful standalone solve, say. It is per-check, reviewed, and "
"visible in the manifest diff. The `manifest` and `license` checks cannot be "
"waived."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:171
msgid ""
"nox -s zoo                          # the whole zoo, both tiers, plus "
"examples\n"
"nox -s zoo -- --zoo-model=my_model  # one model\n"
"nox -s zoo-gating                   # only core-tier models (the merge "
"gate)\n"
"nox -s zoo-community                # only what the gate does not cover "
"(advisory CI)\n"
"nox -s zoo-examples                 # every model's example scripts\n"
"nox -s zoo-docs                     # regenerate docs pages and badges\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:180
msgid ""
"`--zoo-model` and `--zoo-tier` drop the folders they exclude *before* pytest "
"imports anything in them, so a model that fails to import can only fail its "
"own run. That is what keeps the merge gate independent of the community "
"tier: marker deselection alone would not, since it happens after every test "
"module is loaded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:185
msgid ""
"Aim for contract checks under 60 s per model and a model's own tests under 5 "
"minutes; `solve_time` in the manifest is the lever."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:188
msgid "External model collections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:190
msgid ""
"A third-party package can register its own directory of manifests and be "
"discovered by the same registry:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:193
msgid ""
"[project.entry-points.\"pybamm_zoo_models\"]\n"
"my_lab_models = \"my_lab_models\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:198
msgid ""
"It can also hold itself to the `model`-scope contract in its own CI, since "
"the checks ship in `pybamm_model_zoo.testing.contract`. Its models' extras "
"follow the same `zoo-<slug>` naming in the collection's own distribution, "
"and its own `pybamm` requirement is its PyBaMM floor. In-tree models win a "
"name collision, so a third-party package cannot shadow one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:204
msgid "Review checklist for a zoo pull request"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/README.md:206
msgid "Short by design — the contract suite does the rest."
msgstr ""

